A = {
0: """Sure. I work for a large electronics company that makes smartphones and tablets. It's a foreign-invested company, and it's one of the biggest manufacturers in Vietnam. The factory I work at was built about ten years ago in an industrial park in Thai Nguyen province, which is around an hour from Hanoi. When it first opened, people in my hometown were really excited, because it created thousands of jobs for local people. These days, the factory produces millions of devices every year, and most of them are exported to countries all over the world, like the US, Europe, and other parts of Asia. Besides manufacturing, the company also has research and support teams, so there are many different kinds of jobs there. I'm in the quality team, and honestly, I'm proud to work for a company whose products people use every day.""",
1: """Well, my workday usually starts at around a quarter to eight. As soon as I arrive, I change into my uniform, go through the security check, and then I check my email and the production plan for the day. At eight, my team has a short meeting where our leader tells us which models we're checking and whether there were any issues from the night shift. After that, I spend most of the morning on the line, inspecting product samples and recording the results in our system. Lunch is at noon in the company canteen, and that's usually the most relaxing part of the day, because I can chat with friends from other departments. In the afternoon, I do more inspections and sometimes help train new staff. Before I leave, I update my report so the next shift knows what's going on. Most days I finish at five, but when we have urgent orders, I stay a bit later.""",
2: """Last week, I was involved in a small but important project. Our team had to prepare for a customer audit, which means a group of people from a big customer came to check our quality process. It was pretty stressful at first, because we only had about five days to get ready. My job was to review our inspection records and make sure everything was complete and easy to follow. I also helped update a few work instructions that were a little out of date. We had three meetings during the week. In the first one, our manager explained what the customer wanted to see, and in the other two, we checked our progress and practiced answering questions. On the day of the audit, I was nervous, but everything went smoothly, and the customer was satisfied. So in the end, all the late nights were worth it.""",
3: """I live in an apartment on the eighth floor of a building in Thai Nguyen city. It's not very big, but it's cozy and it suits my small family. When you walk in, the first thing you see is the living room. We have a gray sofa, a small coffee table, and a TV on the wall. There's also a big window, so the room gets a lot of natural light in the morning. The kitchen is right next to the living room, and it has everything we need, like a fridge, a stove, and a microwave. Then there are two bedrooms and one bathroom. The bigger bedroom is for my wife and me, and the smaller one belongs to my daughter, and it's always full of toys. What I like most about my apartment is that it's quiet and there's a park just across the street.""",
4: """My routine at home is quite different on weekdays and weekends. On weekdays, I don't spend much time at home, because I work until five. When I get home, I usually take a shower first, and then my wife and I cook dinner together. After dinner, I wash the dishes while my wife helps our daughter with her homework, and later we watch some TV or I read a little before bed. I try to sleep before eleven, but to be honest, that doesn't always happen. Weekends are much more relaxed. On Saturday mornings, I sleep in a bit, and then we do the housework together, like cleaning the floor and doing the laundry. In the afternoon, we often visit my parents or take our daughter to the park. On Sunday evenings, I just relax and get ready for the new week.""",
5: """When I was a child, I lived in a one-story house in a small village with my parents and my grandparents. It was a simple brick house with a living room, two bedrooms, and a kitchen at the back. The best thing about it was the big front yard. There was a mango tree in the middle, and my friends and I used to play football there every afternoon until it got dark. My current home is really different. First of all, I live in an apartment in the city now, so it's much more modern and convenient. We have air conditioning, a washing machine, and a supermarket nearby, which we didn't have back then. On the other hand, my apartment is smaller, and there's no yard, so my daughter has to go to the park to play. I'd say my old house had more space and freedom, but my apartment is more comfortable.""",
6: """Sure. My apartment has a living room, a kitchen, two bedrooms, and a bathroom. The living room is where we spend time together in the evenings, and the kitchen is small but well organized. But my favorite room is actually our bedroom. It's not very big, but I made it really comfortable. When you walk in, you can see a large bed with soft white sheets, and next to it there's a small table with a lamp and a few books. On the other side of the room, there's a desk by the window, where I sometimes work or study English at night. The walls are light blue, and we have some family photos hanging above the bed. I love this room because it's quiet and calm. After a long day at work, lying in bed and reading a little helps me relax completely.""",
7: """Well, keeping the house clean is a team effort in my family. On weekdays, we only do small things, like washing the dishes after dinner, wiping the kitchen table, and putting away my daughter's toys before bed. I'm usually the one who washes the dishes, while my wife does the laundry with the washing machine. On weekends, we do a bigger cleaning. First, I sweep and mop all the floors, and then I clean the bathroom, which is my least favorite job, to be honest. My wife usually changes the bed sheets and organizes the closets. We also water the plants on the balcony and take out the trash and recycling. To keep the house comfortable, we open the windows every morning to let fresh air in. It takes a few hours, but when everything is clean, the whole family feels happier and more relaxed.""",
8: """Last year, we decided to repaint my daughter's bedroom. The old walls were plain white, and after a few years they were covered with pencil marks and stickers, because she loves drawing everywhere. So my wife and I thought it was time for a change. First, we let our daughter choose the color, and of course she picked light pink. Then I went to a hardware store near my house and bought paint, rollers, and some tape. On a Saturday morning, we moved all the furniture to the middle of the room and covered it with plastic sheets. I spent most of the day painting two layers, while my wife took our daughter out so she wouldn't get paint everywhere. It was tiring, but when she came back and saw her pink room, she was so excited. That made all the hard work worth it.""",
9: """Like in any home, we've had a few problems over the years. One of the most common ones is with the water. Our building is a bit old, so sometimes the water pressure is very low, especially in the evening when everyone is cooking and taking showers. Another problem we had was with the air conditioner. Last summer, it suddenly stopped working during a really hot week, and we had to sleep with just a fan for a few days. We've also had small arguments about housework, to be honest. Sometimes my wife thinks I don't clean the kitchen carefully enough, and she's probably right. But we usually talk about it and divide the jobs more clearly. So, these are some of the issues we've had at home, but nothing too serious.""",
10: """Let me tell you about the air conditioner problem. It happened last June, during one of the hottest weeks of the year. One evening, I noticed that the air coming out of the air conditioner wasn't cold anymore, and it was making a strange noise. At first, I thought it just needed cleaning, so I turned it off, removed the filter, and washed it. But when I turned it on again, nothing changed. The next morning, I called the shop where we had bought it. They said a technician could only come in three days because they were very busy. Those three days were really tough, because my daughter couldn't sleep well in the heat, so we put two fans in the bedroom and took cool showers before bed. When the technician finally came, he found that the machine had run out of gas. He refilled it, and it worked perfectly again.""",
11: """There are three people in my family, so we try to share the responsibilities fairly. My wife is mainly in charge of cooking, because she's a much better cook than me, and she also manages the family budget. I'm responsible for washing the dishes, taking out the trash, and fixing anything that breaks around the house. I also take our daughter to kindergarten every morning on my way to work. On weekends, we clean the apartment together. I usually do the floors and the bathroom, and my wife does the laundry and tidies up the bedrooms. Our daughter is only five, but she has small jobs too, like putting away her toys and setting the table before dinner. We don't have a strict schedule, but everyone knows what they need to do, so things usually go smoothly.""",
12: """I'm a big fan of action movies, especially Hollywood action movies. I also enjoy animated films, mostly because I watch them with my daughter. The main reason I like action movies is that they're exciting from beginning to end. When I watch a good car chase or a fight scene, I'm so focused that I forget about everything else, which is a great way to relax after a busy week at work. Another reason is the special effects. These days, movies look so real, and I really respect the effort that goes into making them. For example, I love the Mission: Impossible series, because the main actor does a lot of his own stunts. On the other hand, I don't really enjoy slow romantic movies, because I usually fall asleep halfway through. So if I'm choosing a movie for myself, it's almost always an action movie.""",
13: """The last movie I watched was a Vietnamese comedy about a family that runs a small restaurant. It was about a father who tries to save his restaurant from closing down, and his children all have different ideas about how to do it, which causes a lot of funny situations. I went to see it with my wife last Saturday evening at a theater in a shopping mall near my house. Before the movie, we had a quick dinner at a hot pot place on the same floor, and then we bought some popcorn and two cups of tea. The movie was really funny, and the whole audience laughed a lot. After the movie, we walked around the mall for a while and talked about our favorite scenes. It was a simple date night, but we really enjoyed it because we don't go out alone very often.""",
14: """The most memorable movie for me is Titanic. I watched it on TV with my family when I was about twelve years old. It's a famous love story between a poor young artist and a rich girl, who meet on a huge ship that's traveling across the ocean. In the end, the ship hits an iceberg and sinks, and the man dies to save the woman he loves. What made this movie special for me was that it was the first time a movie made me cry. I remember my whole family sitting in silence at the end. Also, the visual effects were amazing for that time, and the music was beautiful. Even now, whenever I hear the theme song, I remember that evening with my family. I've watched it again a few times as an adult, and it still touches me.""",
15: """I usually go to a movie theater in a big shopping mall in the city center. It's about fifteen minutes from my house by motorbike. The theater is on the top floor of the mall, so before or after a movie, you can go shopping or have something to eat downstairs. When you walk in, there's a large lobby with screens showing the movie schedule, and a counter where you can buy tickets, popcorn, and drinks. Most people buy tickets online now, so it's usually not crowded at the counter. There are about eight screening rooms. They're modern and clean, and the seats are big and comfortable. There's also a special room with couple seats, which my wife likes. The sound system is great, so action movies feel really exciting there. The only downside is that the tickets are a bit expensive on weekends.""",
16: """I listen to many kinds of music, but I mostly enjoy Vietnamese pop and acoustic ballads. Pop music is fun and catchy, so I listen to it when I'm driving or doing housework. Acoustic music is more relaxing, so I usually listen to it in the evening or when I'm tired after work. One of my favorite singers is Den Vau. He's a Vietnamese rapper, but his songs are very gentle and meaningful. His lyrics are about everyday life, like working hard, missing your hometown, or spending time with friends, so I can really relate to them. I also like some international artists, like Ed Sheeran, because his voice is warm and his songs are easy to sing along to. To be honest, I'm not a big fan of heavy rock or electronic music, because it's too loud for me.""",
17: """I listen to music almost every day, but mostly at certain times. In the morning, I listen to upbeat songs on my phone while I'm commuting, because it helps me wake up and get ready for work. In the evening, after dinner, I sometimes play relaxing music on a small speaker in the living room while my family is reading or playing. I don't really listen to the radio anymore, except when I'm in a taxi or in my father's car, because he always has the radio on. As for concerts, I don't go very often, because tickets can be expensive and the big concerts are usually in Hanoi. But I try to go to one or two live shows a year with my friends. I also love singing karaoke, so whenever we have a party, we usually end up singing together.""",
18: """I first became interested in music when I was in middle school. My older cousin had a lot of CDs, and whenever I visited his house, we listened to them together. At that time, I mostly liked Vietnamese pop songs, and I tried to learn the lyrics of every song I heard on TV. In high school, my taste changed a little, because my friends were really into Korean pop, so I started following some K-pop groups too. After I started working, though, I found that I needed calmer music. My job can be stressful, so these days I mostly listen to acoustic songs and ballads. I still enjoy pop music at parties, but I don't follow new songs as closely as I used to. So my interest in music hasn't really gone away, it has just become more relaxed as I've grown older.""",
19: """I remember a New Year's Eve concert I went to about two years ago. It was held in a big square in the center of Hanoi, and I went there with three of my close friends from university. We arrived early, around seven o'clock, but the square was already packed with thousands of people. There were many famous singers performing, and the atmosphere was amazing. Everyone was singing along and dancing to the music. What made it so memorable was the countdown at midnight. When the clock hit twelve, the singers on stage started a song that we all loved when we were students, and then fireworks lit up the whole sky. My friends and I hugged each other and took a lot of photos. It was crowded and very noisy, and it took us almost an hour to get out, but it was one of the best nights I've ever had.""",
20: """I usually go to two kinds of parks. The first one is a small neighborhood park just across the street from my apartment. It has a short walking path, some benches under big trees, and a small playground for kids, so it's perfect for a quick walk after dinner. The second one is a bigger city park, about fifteen minutes away by motorbike. It's built around a large lake, and there's a paved path around it that's great for jogging. Along the path, there are lots of trees, flower beds, and some outdoor exercise machines. On one side of the lake, there's also a bigger playground and an open lawn where families have picnics on the weekends. I like both parks, but for different reasons. The small one is convenient, and the big one is more relaxing and beautiful.""",
21: """A typical visit to the park for me is pretty simple. I usually go in the evening, after dinner, with my wife and daughter. When we arrive, my daughter runs straight to the playground, because she loves the slides and the swings. While she plays, my wife and I sit on a bench nearby and chat about our day. After that, we usually take a walk around the lake together. There are always lots of people there. You can see older people doing exercise or dancing to music, teenagers playing badminton, and couples taking photos. Sometimes there are street vendors selling ice cream or balloons, and my daughter always asks for one. We usually stay for about an hour, and then we walk home. It's a small routine, but it helps me relax and spend quality time with my family.""",
22: """The last time I went to a park was last Sunday morning. I went to the big park near the city center with my wife and daughter. We arrived at around seven, when the weather was still cool. First, we walked around the lake for about thirty minutes. It was really peaceful, because there was a light breeze and the trees were very green after the rain the night before. After that, my daughter wanted to play at the playground, so we stayed there for a while, and I pushed her on the swing. Then we bought some sticky rice from a vendor near the gate and had a little breakfast on a bench by the lake. Before leaving, we fed the fish in the lake, which my daughter loved. We left around nine, when it started to get hot. It was a simple morning, but it was really refreshing.""",
23: """I started going to parks when I was a university student in Hanoi. At that time, I lived in a small rented room with two friends, and it was really hot and noisy, so in the evenings we often went to a park nearby just to get some fresh air and escape from the crowded room. We used to sit by the lake, chat, and sometimes play badminton. That's how parks became a part of my life. These days, my reasons are a bit different. Now I mainly go to parks for my health and for my family. I try to walk or jog a few times a week to stay in shape, because I sit a lot at work. Also, my daughter loves the playground, so going to the park is a great way for us to spend time together without spending any money.""",
24: """I remember something unexpected that happened at a park about a year ago. It was a Saturday evening, and I took my daughter to the big park near the city center. That day, there was a lantern festival for the Mid-Autumn holiday, so the park was much more crowded than usual. While we were watching a lion dance performance, my daughter let go of my hand for just a second, and suddenly I couldn't see her anymore. I panicked and started calling her name and looking everywhere. After about ten minutes, which felt like forever, I heard an announcement from a speaker saying that a little girl was waiting at the information booth. When I got there, she was holding a lantern and eating candy that the staff gave her, totally calm. I was so relieved. Since then, I always hold her hand tightly in crowded places.""",
25: """I usually go for walks around the lake in a park near my house. I go about three or four times a week, mostly in the evening after work, because the weather is cooler then. Before I go, I put on comfortable sneakers and bring a small bottle of water. While I'm walking, I like to listen to music or a podcast, sometimes in English to practice my listening. Usually I walk for about forty-five minutes, at a pretty fast pace. On the way, I see lots of people doing exercise, and sometimes I meet my neighbors and stop to chat for a few minutes. After a walk, I always feel refreshed and much calmer. It helps me forget about the stress from work, and I also sleep much better at night. So for me, walking is the easiest way to stay healthy and relaxed.""",
26: """The last time I went for a walk was yesterday evening. After dinner, I checked the weather on my phone to make sure it wasn't going to rain, put on my sneakers, and grabbed my earphones and a bottle of water. I walked to the park near my house, which only takes about five minutes. That evening, I decided to walk two rounds around the lake, which is about three kilometers. Halfway through, I ran into an old friend from high school who I hadn't seen for years. He had just moved to my neighborhood, so we walked together for the rest of the way and caught up on each other's lives. It was a nice surprise. After the walk, I went home, took a shower, and drank a glass of water. Then I sat on the sofa and felt really relaxed before going to bed.""",
27: """I started taking walks about five years ago, mainly because of my health. At that time, I had just started working in an office, and I sat in front of a computer for most of the day. I gained a few kilos, and I often felt tired and had back pain. A doctor told me I needed to move more, so I started walking in the evenings. At first, I only walked for about twenty minutes, and honestly, it felt a bit boring. But after a few weeks, I noticed that I slept better and felt less stressed, so I kept going. Over the years, walking has become more than just exercise. Now it's my quiet time to think, listen to music, or spend time with my family. These days, I walk not only to stay healthy but also to clear my mind after work.""",
28: """My favorite beach is Sam Son beach in Thanh Hoa province. It's about four hours from my house by car, so I usually go there in the summer with my family. The beach is very long and wide, with soft yellow sand and fairly calm waves, so it's a good place for kids to swim. Along the beach, there's a long road with lots of hotels, restaurants, and small shops selling souvenirs and swimsuits. In the evening, the whole area is full of lights and street food stalls, so it's very lively. At one end of the beach, there's a small mountain with a temple on top, and you can climb up and see a beautiful view of the sea. The only downside is that it gets very crowded in the summer, but I still love the atmosphere there.""",
29: """When I go to the beach, I like to do lots of different activities. In the early morning, I usually get up around five to watch the sunrise and take a walk along the shore while it's still cool. After breakfast, I go swimming in the sea with my family. My daughter loves building sandcastles and collecting shells, so I often help her with that. Around noon, when the sun is too strong, we go back to the hotel to rest and have lunch. In the late afternoon, we go back to the beach and sometimes play volleyball or just relax under an umbrella with a cold drink. In the evening, my favorite thing is eating fresh seafood at a restaurant near the beach. After dinner, we usually walk around the night market. It's a perfect way to relax and recharge.""",
}
